{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"My dearest Marie,\n\nI am settled at the Hôtel des Princes, a decent enough room for the price, though the air is thick. I saw Cousin this evening; he is still chattering about \"spirit\" as if he had invented it, which is amusing given our own work. We walked the Boulevards later. The Palais Royal is a labyrinth of small shops, and the Tuileries were quiet. But the Champs Élysées! It is a spectacle. The Ambassadeurs and Aurore are packed with families, children spinning on carousels, coffee being drunk in great quantities. It feels less like a city and more like a large, noisy market for the soul.\n\nThe food here is light; I ate a simple soup and some bread, perhaps too little. I am tired. The journey from Berlin has worn me down. I miss the stillness of our house and the sound of the boys’ voices. I shall rest now. Do not worry; I am well, just far away.\n\nYour loving Georg"}}],"created":1795219242,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"completion_tokens":217,"prompt_tokens":1131,"total_tokens":1348,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0}},"id":"chatcmpl-OKRiHhWj9gtOf2ahjfwR61OwNCHZz0Hs","timings":{"cache_n":0,"prompt_n":1131,"prompt_ms":1070.013,"prompt_per_token_ms":0.946076923076923,"prompt_per_second":1056.9965037807954,"predicted_n":217,"predicted_ms":5119.25,"predicted_per_token_ms":23.70023148148148,"predicted_per_second":42.19368071494848}}